<title>USA: Maine lawmakers to start public budget hearings.</title>
<headline>Maine lawmakers to start public budget hearings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the Maine legislature's budget writing panel plan to start public hearings Monday on the nearly $4 billion, two-year budget proposed by Gov. Angus King.</p>
<p>They want to finish work by April 1.</p>
<p>The appropriations committee hopes to complete hearings by the end of the month. The items scheduled to be discussed first are the state's higher education institutions and the Department of Education.</p>
<p>King's plan to phase out state aid to the magnet school in Limestone is expected to draw a crowd.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
